iMac 5K: halt the tiled resync worker when the machine is going down

Companion to 5k-post-commit-link-recovery.patch, as a separate patch because
amdgpu_dm_apple5k_going_down() sits at a different file position in the lean
core and the verbose stack, and GNU patch locates hunks in file order -- one
patch cannot carry this hunk for both stacks.

Set the worker's stopping flag and cancel it at the same point where the
going-down gate is raised, so a pending link-health pass cannot fire while
the display is being torn down for firmware.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
@@ -2999,6 +2999,11 @@
 void amdgpu_dm_apple5k_going_down(struct amdgpu_device *adev)
 {
-	if (adev && adev->dm.dc)
+	if (adev && adev->dm.dc) {
+		mutex_lock(&adev->dm.dc_lock);
+		adev->dm.tiled_resync_stopping = true;
 		adev->dm.dc->apple_5k_going_down = true;
+		mutex_unlock(&adev->dm.dc_lock);
+		cancel_delayed_work_sync(&adev->dm.tiled_resync_work);
+	}
 }

